            <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-sm mb-2 text-cyan-400">Choose Standalone TensorRT When:</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300">
              <li>• Deploying on fixed NVIDIA hardware with zero heterogeneous targets</li>
              <li>• Every single microsecond counts (real-time robotics, sub-5ms vision)</li>
              <li>• Batch inference is fully fixed with static dimensions</li>
              <li>• Your deployment pipeline has pre-compiled engine delivery</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-emerald-500/20">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-sm mb-2 text-emerald-400">Choose ONNX Runtime (TRT EP) When:</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300">
              <li>• Fleet consists of mixed hardware (NVIDIA GPUs, Intel CPUs, Apple NPUs)</li>
              <li>• Models contain dynamic shapes or unsupported custom layers</li>
              <li>• You require seamless fallback to CUDA or CPU on engine build failure</li>
              <li>• Engineering velocity and unified C#/Python/Rust bindings matter</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <div class="pt-8 border-t border-slate-800">
